From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Faster load, lazy icons

webots-bin links the system zlib ahead of assimp, which exports an old
bundled copy that PNG decoding otherwise bound to. A world's local
PNG and JPEG files (image textures, the background's terrain detail
and light layers) start decoding on a thread pool before its nodes
finalize one after the other; each node takes its file's image when it
needs it. Toolbar and menu icons (512-pixel images, enabled and
disabled) are decoded the first time they are drawn in that state, not
all at start. Same decoders, same pixels.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0049-system-zlib-first: forest load 12.8 -> 11.0 s
- 0059-lazy-button-icons: RAM 719 -> 655 MB
- 0061-image-prefetch: forest load 9.5 -> 8.0 s
